  "9:41",
  "三0口",
  "< Back",
  "Dementia Care Services",
  "Welcome to the Dementia Services section",
  "Caring for a person living with dementia can be",
  "challenging. It can affect your emotions, your",
  "health, your time, and your finances. You are not",
  "alone - many services are available to support",
  "you and your family.",
  "This section helps you find dementia-related",
  "services near you in a simple way.",
  "To get started:",
  "• The map will automatically show services",
  "near the address in your profile",
  "• If you want to search in a different area, type",
  "a new address into the \"Search location\" box",
  "• You can choose different types of services",
  "(for example, hospitals, respite care, or peer",
  "support)",
  "• You can also adjust how far from your",
  "location you would like to search",
  "Dementia care often requires different types of",
  "support. Services you may find helpful include:",
  "• Government-funded aged care services",
  "• Disability support services (for people",
  "diagnosed before age 65)",
  "• Carer support, including counselling and",
  "peer support",
  "• Help to support your loved one at home",
  "• Specialist services for managing behaviour",
  "changes",
  "• Respite care, so you can take a break",
  "We understand that language and cultural needs",
  "are important. Some services may offer",
  "interpreters or culturally appropriate",
  "care - please check with the service provider.",
  "For more information about support services,",
  "please see Module 6 in the iSupport course.",
